  "body": "## What changed\n\nA planned corner relief whose start no pass vertex reaches, and for which no legal detour exists, was dropped without a diagnostic (#3249). It could leave material the operator does not expect.\n\n- `inject_relief_spurs` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs`) now reports each skipped relief: the caller gets the boundary corners in a `misses` vector.\n- The pocket emit path (`pocket_emit.rs`) and the pocket avoid path (`pocket_avoid.rs`) write one note per corner into the `PathBuilder` / path notes: `corner relief at (x, y) is not cut: no pass vertex reaches the relief spur`. Notes are de-duplicated by corner, so a multi-level cut or a retry names each corner once.\n- The four-dogbones rest test keeps its no-note assert: a reached relief adds no note.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket corner relief that no pass reaches is now named in the operation notes instead of being dropped silently.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `machining2d::corner_relief_spur::tests::a_relief_no_pass_reaches_is_reported_as_a_miss` (crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief_spur.rs): the miss is reported and no spur is spliced in; a reached relief reports no miss and gets its spur.\n- `unreachable_corners_and_bad_overrides_are_refused` (crates/motion/tests/corner_relief.rs): the island-blocked spur refuses at plan time.\n- `crates/motion/tests/rest_corner_relief.rs`: the rest pass keeps its no-note assert.\n\n## Review fix\n\nThe miss vector uses `r.corner`, the boundary corner, instead of `r.start`, the cutter-center start.\nBoth existing callers use the returned corners for duplicate detection.\n\n- The existing miss pin now uses corner `(0,0)` and start `(3,3)`.\n- `machining2d::pocket_emit::tests::missed_relief_notes_name_and_deduplicate_boundary_corners` checks the resulting path notes.\n  It checks equal corners with different starts and different corners with an equal start.\n\n## Review fix validation\n\nFinal head: `1814e1119b8fdbf86f1f6a4fe8b245b9a30286e0`.\nBase: `9dfcc7ac2ae59c30a43796382968b4cba93970e5` (`upstream/main`).\n\nThe base was fetched before these checks. Upstream advanced during the run to `6167d30af724eb8fa8904b6744c26cd295ff08dd`.\nAfter fetching that head, both dry plans were compared with the recorded base.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --dry-run` selects the same nine step names and commands.\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` selects the same 243 step names and commands.\n`git diff --name-only <base>...HEAD` lists the same five files for both bases.\nThe completed checks cover every step selected against current upstream/main. No additional step was selected.\nThe actual runs used base `9dfcc7ac2ae59c30a43796382968b4cba93970e5`. A merge with newer main was not exercised.\n\nThe miss vector now contains boundary corners. Existing callers use these points to remove duplicate notes.\nThe path-note test checks equal corners with different starts and different corners with an equal start.\n\nPin proof:\n\n- `machining2d::corner_relief_spur::tests::a_relief_no_pass_reaches_is_reported_as_a_miss`\n- `machining2d::pocket_emit::tests::missed_relief_notes_name_and_deduplicate_boundary_corners`\n\nEach pin passed with the fix. Changing `misses.push(r.corner)` back to `misses.push(r.start)` made both pins fail.\nThe first pin reported `(3,3)` instead of `(0,0)`. The path-note pin reported `(3,3)` and `(4,3)` instead of `(0,0)` and `(10,0)`.\nRestoring the fix made both pins pass again. Commands used `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib <full_test_name> -- --exact`.\n\nFinal-head checks:\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=16 cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 9 steps passed, 0 failed, 5.0 minutes.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache cargo clippy -j 16 -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --no-fail-fast --test example_catalog --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work --test first_part_programs --test first_router_part --test first_4axis_part --test continuous_4axis_part --test catalog_groove_part_off -- --test-threads=16`: passed. 60 tests passed, 4 ignored. `example_catalog` had 37 passed and 4 ignored in debug. The heavy run passed all four ignored catalog tests in release.\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=16 cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 243 steps passed, 0 failed, 39.0 minutes. All reached motion and app heavy targets ran. Four registered known-fail checks failed as expected and passed their gate checks.\n\nGoldens moved: none. The catalog and recorded-program checks above passed without changes. No recorded program changed. The heavy stock-engine checks also passed for every golden program.\n\nThe first quick run failed after automatic target seeding copied stale build artifacts. A package-only clean did not clear the full dependency chain.\nA worktree debug-profile clean and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` resolved the build errors. The final quick run passed.\nNo source or dependency changed for this recovery.\n\nUI screenshots: not applicable. This fix changes no UI.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The note text in a posted NC program through the full post pipeline.\n- The avoid-path note on a multi-level cut with more than one skipped corner.\n\nFork synced at v0.25.0\n\nFixes #3249\n\n",
